    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πη</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>somewhere, anywhere</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλη πη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Berl.Sitzb.</u>
					1927
				</span></i>
			. 
			<i><span class="en">
				167
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cyrene</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> indirect interrog. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῆ</span></b> , <i>where</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴσατι πῆ ἐστι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
					4.70
				</span></i>
			 (
				Locr.
			 Epizeph.); cf. sq. <i><span class="en">
				B.
				11.2
			</span></i>. (Panhellenic <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span> and no iota, cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήποκα</span>.)</div>
